# CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request a review from the listed owner(s)
# whenever a PR touches a matching path, and (if you turn on the branch
# protection rule "Require review from Code Owners") to block merging
# without that review.
#
# Syntax: a path pattern (same rules as .gitignore), then one or more
# owners (a GitHub username or team, with an @). Later rules override
# earlier ones for the same path, so keep the most general rule first and
# more specific overrides below it — exactly like the layout here.
#
# Replace @Omkekan below with your actual GitHub username if this isn't
# it, and add teams/other owners here as the project grows past one person.

# Default: one owner for everything not matched more specifically below.
*   @Omkekan

# Anything security-sensitive gets called out explicitly, even though it
# currently resolves to the same owner — this is what you extend first
# once a second person joins, so auth/credential/scope-policy changes
# always get an extra set of eyes before merging.
/backend/src/riskreveal/core/security.py                  @Omkekan
/backend/src/riskreveal/domain/credentials/                @Omkekan
/backend/src/riskreveal/domain/scanning/scope_policy.py     @Omkekan
/backend/src/riskreveal/domain/scanning/authorization.py    @Omkekan
/backend/src/riskreveal/config.py                           @Omkekan

# Infra and CI changes — also worth a deliberate second look once there's
# a second person, since these affect what every contributor's CI run does.
/infra/                      @Omkekan
/.github/                    @Omkekan
